# Scratch captures from the Shape Space tab — unregistered objects grabbed for
# exploration, never corpus material (their target_ids are not in targets_v1.csv,
# and a corpus build hard-errors on those by design)
src/data/scratch/

# Superseded calibration profiles — kept on disk, not repo source. Only the
# current *operating* profile is tracked (§10 firmware<->ML contract); it is
# cal_3x10_v1.json, deliberately absent from this list.
#
# Listed file-by-file rather than as `src/data/profiles/*` + a negation: the
# wildcard form is correct as far as git is concerned, but the dir/* + !negation
# idiom renders unreliably in some editors' ignore decorations. The trade-off is
# that new delaycal candidate profiles are NOT ignored by default — add each
# superseded lock here as it is retired.
src/data/profiles/cal_63_air_bat_v3.json
src/data/profiles/cal_63_air_v1.json
src/data/profiles/cal_63_air_v2.json
src/data/profiles/cal_72_air_v2.json
src/data/profiles/cal_72_air_v3.json

# (2026-08-09) The ML/, References/V3/, References/Targets v1 Analysis/ and
# utilities/ rules that stood here are gone with the directories themselves —
# all four were retired at the cal_3x10_v1 epoch turnover. References/ now holds
# only images/. Nothing is ignored in its place: a rule guarding a path that no
# longer exists is worse than no rule, because it reads as though the thing is
# still there and merely untracked.
